<%= page_nav :contact, "Contact · HTMX on Rails" %>

<section class="page-head">
  <h1>Contact</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A form that never leaves the page. The browser validates nothing
    (<code>novalidate</code>) so you can watch Rails answer with
    <code>422</code> and re-rendered errors, or with a success card.
  </p>
</section>

<div class="grid grid-2">
  <div>
    <%= render "pages/contact_card", message: @message %>
  </div>

  <section class="card">
    <header class="card-head">
      <h2>On the wire</h2>
      <span class="tag">HX-*</span>
    </header>
    <ul class="notes">
      <li>
        <code>data-hx-post</code> + <code>data-hx-target="#contact-card"</code> +
        <code>data-hx-swap="outerHTML"</code> — htmx submits the form and replaces
        the card with whatever the server returns.
        <code>data-hx-disabled-elt="find button"</code> disables the submit button
        for the duration.
      </li>
      <li>
        The CSRF token rides along in <code>data-hx-headers</code> on
        <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>, inherited by every htmx request on the page.
      </li>
      <li>
        A valid post answers with <code>HX-Trigger: contact:message-sent</code>;
        <code>app/javascript/application.js</code> listens for that DOM event and
        shows the toast in the corner.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <%= code_sample :form %>
    <%= code_sample :csrf %>
  </section>
</div>
